{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_03c_resolved_and_unresolved_failures", "label": "03c-resolved-and-unresolved-failures.md", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "page", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11-testing/06-mockmvc/03c-resolved-and-unresolved-failures.md", "source_location": "L1", "frontmatter": {"title": "An exception in a handler puts a MockMvc test into one of two states \u2014 resolved, where a HandlerExceptionResolver produced a response you can assert on, and unresolved, where nothing did and there is therefore no response at all \u2014 and the classic API throws it out of perform() while MockMvcTester hands you a result object that throws only when you touch it", "sidebar_label": "03c \u00b7 Resolved and unresolved failures", "sidebar_position": "7"}, "_origin": "ast"}, {"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_03c_resolved_and_unresolved_failures_resolved_and_unresolved_the_distinction_with_no_name_in_most_codebases", "label": "\ud83d\udd34 Resolved and unresolved \u2014 the distinction with no name in most codebases", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11-testing/06-mockmvc/03c-resolved-and-unresolved-failures.md", "source_location": "L28", "_origin": "ast"}, {"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_03c_resolved_and_unresolved_failures_how_each_api_surfaces_it", "label": "How each API surfaces it", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11-testing/06-mockmvc/03c-resolved-and-unresolved-failures.md", "source_location": "L53", "_origin": "ast"}, {"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_03c_resolved_and_unresolved_failures_the_trap_hasfailed_covers_both_states_but_the_assertions_after_it_do_not", "label": "\ud83d\udd34 The trap: `hasFailed()` covers both states, but the assertions after it do not", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11